{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/804996-looking-for-a-new-player","id":804996,"title":"Looking for a new Player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-09T21:22:50-08:00","id":804996,"title":"Looking for a new Player","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Hey everybody, I'm running a game on Thursday nights (8 - 12 EST) on Skype, using text. We lost our third player a few sessions into our second story, and we are just coming to the end of it now, so I am hoping to find a replacement. The actual details for this game are all below, including an example of our most resent session for people to check out to see if it interests them. Toss me a PM, or put a post here if you're interested or have any questions.</span> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Pots and Pans</span></span></span></b></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>A month ago, something happened. No one knows for sure what, but England roared with thunderous hoofbeats, and out of the mist a fleet of rotting reed ships sailed the Celtic Sea. In a single month, England has been brought under the rule of Arthur Pendragon, and those of his knights who did not betray him. Ireland, on the other hand, has been placed under the beautiful but tyrannical heel of Bres, son of Elatha. </i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>Brittany</i></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i> and Normandy both have had entire forests appear overnight, on land that didn't exist the day before, and there are whispers of enchanting things lurking there.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>For now, the rest of the world watches on in confusion, diplomatic relationships trying to be harbored with the new Ard Ri of an Ireland unified under a tyrannical boot, and the returned King of England. No monsters lurk in Grecian woods, the city beneath the streets of Mexico City lies buried and quiet, all but England and Ireland are simple and mundane for the time.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>You, one of the exceptionally rare Scions of the world, barely more than a mortal, have been called upon by your Divine Parent, or maybe a concerned Pantheon member, and gifted Power in exchange for a service.</i></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><i>Travel to Lac Chauvet, France, and wait. Wait, watch, and learn what has happened.</i></span></span></span> <hr /> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Band</span></span></b></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Aisling</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: A beautiful woman, born of a tryst between Fand and Lancelot, and fostered by her Step-Father Manannan mac Lir. A musical soul, blessed with the light of the summer, and incredible luck. Aisling has a heart kind enough to lift even the most tormented of spirits, including Brigid who was hiding in a secret cloister in sorrow for her slain son. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Powers</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Epic Appearance, Epic Charisma, Illusion, Magic, Sun.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Grant</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: A wise son of Hades, Grant has been tasked with discovering the secrets of the \u2018stone bones\u2019 and how to breathe life back into them by his father for unspoken reasons. A paleontologist, Grant is as tough as stone, wielding his father\u2019s authority over death, and the earth, adding his own skills of bird and beast. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Powers</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: Animal, Death Earth, Epic Intelligence, Epic Manipulation</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Various Notes</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This game is being used to test the Heroic (and soon Demigod) Powers written for Scion 2.0, so there will likely be various moments of rejigging effects slightly, and altering costs. Due to using this game as a tester for the revised Purviews we have written, I would prefer to not double up on any Purviews, or character concepts just to get as wide a breadth of Boons tested as possible. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So far, the game has 22 Sessions encompassing two Stories (we will likely finish Story 2 in one more session just to wrap everything up). We play from 8pm - 12am EST on Thursday nights. We play with Skype through text, and use MIRC with a dice script to manage our rolling. For an example of how we play, </span></span><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kxc2L_u9zfhEWBkEeaxpHT0BgUUOHHTaTVBjk3dQnj8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>here</u></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> is our most recent Session.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Character Creation</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Just so people get an idea of the differences and limitations we are using, I want to give a quick rundown on the character creation. Our base rules for character creation are found </span></span><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home/character-creation\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>here</u></span></span></a><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, with the addition that a new character is starting at Legend 4, with 219 experience, including the base 45 all characters start with.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Past the previously mentioned limits on Powers, there is also a slight limitation on Pantheon. The story of the game is focused on a very strange series of events that have linked at minimum five of the Western European Pantheons as far as the players have discovered (The Tuatha, the Aesir, the Theoi, the Nemetondevos [unplayable], and the Duwiau [the Welsh, also unplayable]). People are absolutely welcome to play a character from a more distant Pantheon with the understanding that while their Pantheon would be woven into the story, they would be less involved in themes and likely have less direct involvement. The only Pantheon I outright ban is the Bogovi, but only because there is no Titan War or a similar situation to warrant the Pantheon breaking their rules about half-mortal children. Several Pantheons are not complete or updated for Scion 2.0, but depending on the Pantheon, we can probably get something sorted out.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 01-10-2016, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:35:22-08:00","id":805445,"title":"","content":"Definitely interested in playing, and luckily Thursday nights are usually my least busy so I'm good there. I've actually got a couple ideas already (either a Scion of Marduk or Thor probably) so hopefully it won't take long for me to get a character made up for you to look at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4010-thenotorioussmp","name":"TheNotoriousSMP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-10T13:53:53-08:00","id":805461,"title":"","content":"Wicked, I look forward to seeing what you come up with.<br /> <br /> I entirely forgot to actually provide <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1RL3COCw0fx06QDFhE-3t_-uJUYe5x0_rGZOczxZU6_U/edit\" target=\"_blank\">character sheets</a> (just make a copy under file), and an <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1y1RmQGzEbw8OnW_PU6BdOM0YSmjk-pL1_Uy8zeGY7Ko/edit\" target=\"_blank\">example filled out sheet</a> since several of the boxes on the blank sheet just presume people know what goes in there. I'll throw you a PM here in a moment with a little extra information that you might need for creating a character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T09:07:17-08:00","id":806137,"title":"","content":"Ah, too bad.<br /> <br /> I certainly would have loved to play, but I'm in Europe, so Thursday evenings are too late for me. <br /> <br /> Have fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-13T10:43:41-08:00","id":808026,"title":"","content":"I'm sorry about that Evilmarmelade! Different time zones are exceptionally tricky, I'm sorry that our time doesn't work out for you. <br /> <br /> I am sure we defiantly will enjoy things! Hopefully next time we are looking for people we'll have a time that would be more viable for folks outside of the Americas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/